      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to simplify the expression \\(\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3}\\) and express it in the form \\(a \\sqrt[4]{b}\\), where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are positive integers. We will then find \\(a + b\\).\n\nFirst, we start by expressing the given radical in a more manageable form:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3}\n\\]\n\nWe can rewrite the expression as:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3} = \\sqrt[4]{2^7} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{3^3}\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify \\(\\sqrt[4]{2^7}\\) and \\(\\sqrt[4]{3^3}\\) individually.\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\sqrt[4]{2^7}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7} = 2^{7/4}\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\sqrt[4]{3^3}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{3^3} = 3^{3/4}\n\\]\n\nCombining these, we get:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3} = 2^{7/4} \\cdot 3^{3/4}\n\\]\n\nThis can be rewritten as:\n\\[\n2^{7/4} \\cdot 3^{3/4} = (2^7 \\cdot 3^3)^{1/4}\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the values inside the parentheses:\n\\[\n2^7 = 128 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 3^3 = 27\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n2^7 \\cdot 3^3 = 128 \\cdot 27\n\\]\n\nWe multiply these values:\n\\[\n128 \\cdot 27 = 128 \\cdot (30 - 3) = 128 \\cdot 30 - 128 \\cdot 3 = 3840 - 384 = 3456\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3} = 3456^{1/4}\n\\]\n\nWe need to express \\(3456^{1/4}\\) in the form \\(a \\sqrt[4]{b}\\). We can express 3456 as a power of 2 and 3:\n\\[\n3456 = 2^7 \\cdot 3^3\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n3456^{1/4} = (2^7 \\cdot 3^3)^{1/4} = 2^{7/4} \\cdot 3^{3/4}\n\\]\n\nWe already know that:\n\\[\n2^{7/4} = 2 \\cdot 2^{3/4} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 3^{3/4} = \\sqrt[4]{27}\n\\]\n\nSo:\n\\[\n3456^{1/4} = 2 \\cdot 2^{3/4} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{27}\n\\]\n\nIn the form \\(a \\sqrt[4]{b}\\), we have:\n\\[\na = 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad b = 27\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\\[\na + b = 2 + 27 = 29\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{29}\n\\]",
